==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*3 [[Duche]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 26.67~40 seconds<sup>800f~1,200f</sup>.
*3 [[Owlbrow]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Teacher Bun Bun]] spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
**8 [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**10 [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
**10 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The Metal Doges aren't as much of a threat as they seem, so instead of bringing critical hitters, bring 3-4 meatshields. The other peons can be dealt with by spammable Area Attackers such as [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], and [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]]. Teacher Bun Bun can make quick work of your stack, so bring [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|Anti-Floating Cats]] such as [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Bishop Cat]], [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Shaman Cat]], and [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Kotatsu Cat]] to minimize its pushing power.

